WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.110
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:15.750
Last time: Input → Process → Output

3
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:22.200
Chapter 3 · Robots & Automation

4
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:31.940
Au · to · ma · tion. Another big word!

5
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:43.280
Meet Bolt, the robot waiter!

6
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:52.740
Bolt brings your dosa, then rolls back

7
00:00:52.740 --> 00:01:03.460
Is Bolt happy? Does she like her job?

8
00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:15.080
Bolt doesn't feel. The smile is just a picture.

9
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:22.930
Robot = a machine that follows instructions

10
00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:37.880
Bolt's algorithm: Go · Give the plate · Come back

11
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:50.290
No steps? The robot doesn't know what to do

12
00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:59.960
Automation: a machine does a job by itself

13
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:14.200
Forward, turn. Forward, turn. Again and again!

14
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:23.220
Repeating the same steps = a LOOP

15
00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:37.310
Repeat: forward, turn… until clean

16
00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:47.320
A factory arm fixes the same part on every car

17
00:02:47.320 --> 00:03:01.050
Pick up box, put on belt… again and again

18
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:11.600
Robots are great at repeat jobs!

19
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:24.400
Oh no! Juice spilled on the floor!

20
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:33.150
What will Bolt do? Think!

21
00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:45.400
Bolt just keeps following her steps

22
00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:56.400
New, messy jobs? People do better!

23
00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:03.180
Game: Robot CAN or robot CAN'T?

24
00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:19.970
Which jobs can a robot do?

25
00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:36.300
Repeat jobs: CAN. Ideas & feelings: CAN'T

26
00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:43.270
Home robot: sweeps your room

27
00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:48.530
Factory robot: builds cars, packs boxes

28
00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:54.210
Space robot: a rover on Mars

29
00:04:54.210 --> 00:05:01.190
Same idea: they all follow instructions

30
00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:20.840
Pick up can → Walk → ??? → Walk back

31
00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:26.880
Step 3: tip the can to pour water!

32
00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.830
Your turn: practice check

33
00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:42.130
Why can't a vacuum robot invent a new game?

34
00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:55.230
It only follows steps. No steps for new games!

35
00:05:55.230 --> 00:06:03.040
Robots follow algorithms. They don't feel.

36
00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:07.210
Great at repeat jobs: loops!

37
00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:11.540
Poor at new, messy jobs without steps

38
00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:17.630
Home · Factory · Space: same idea

39
00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:23.840
Chapter 3 done!

40
00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:30.640
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
